It is a good game.
Pros:
- Beautiful environment, city, characters and other general pictures;
- Interesting story with small twists, very good on the sci-fi story for any fan;
- customized combos, dynamic battle mechanics, but could be better;
- dynamic music, it growths with the game and fights;
- amazning concept artistic transformation in the game itseft.
Cons:
- repetitive battles;
- lack of new enemies, basic the same sprites with new image/face;
- climbing and walking in a pre determinated path, no illussion of choice as there is only 1 way all the time;
- short game, just a few hours while it promises much more;
- no puzzles, no labirynth, no discovery;

Simply put, the game might be fun, but it's VERY buggy and glitchy:
- freezing/crashing;
- resetting settings on alt+tab and every time you restart the game;
- randomly forgets it's supposed to be fullscreen and goes in borderless windowed mode with top left corner in the middle of the screen;
- quest npc's getting stuck;
- unintuitive and infuriating controlscheme (both on controller and mouse/keyboard) that can't be rebound;
- a 100.000 items that have to be scrolls through to select a gun, while being chased by multile enemies that just crawled from the ground (and the character stops running when selecting certain items);
- aiming a gun doesn't fire at reticle, have to be moving for that to work for some reason;
- combat mechanics are all-round horrible;
- so many light beams showing quest objectives (or whatever) that are deep underground and can't be found (even by digging, they're apparently below the world);
Next to that, mouse/keyboard controls are HORRIBLE!! Just horrible, ♥♥♥♥♥♥♥♥ keybindings that can't be changed (attack and run are both on the left mouse-button for some reason?) I can not recommend this game to anyone who's not keen on playing with a controller.

