This review comes a few months after I finished the game, but I very much liked this game.  It gives a very wonderfully conclusive 'What if?' approach to the series, perhaps in response to the displeasure some fans felt over the ending of the prior game.  The gameplay is just as in the prior series, with charming writing and characters throughout.  There isn't much in the way of innovation, as much as just more good writing that doesn't wear thin thanks to to its alternate take on the series.  If any complaint could be made, its that the game is a bit more linear than the prior games, but it doesnt make the game less enjoyable in my experience.
There's also no Chorus Guys songs for every chapter. Doh.  I loved em. ;v;
It may also may sway my opinion sharply that I am a bit of a sucker for good time travel stories, and in my opinion, this is a good one.

